From: Sebastian Huang <sebastian_huang@accton.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtk: mac80211: keep the deflink of a non-MLD AP_VLAN

"mtk: mac80211: remove links when removing AP_VLAN interface" clears
all links of an AP_VLAN when it is removed, also when the AP_VLAN is
not an MLD. For a non-MLD interface link 0 is the deflink, and its
group keys use link ID 0. With link 0 cleared, ieee80211_key_replace()
returns -ENOLINK for them before unlinking, ieee80211_do_stop() frees
them anyway, and ieee80211_teardown_sdata() then walks the stale key
list:

  Unable to handle kernel ... at virtual address 0000000000001238
  pc : ieee80211_key_replace (key.c: sdata->link[link_id])
   ieee80211_free_keys_iface
   ieee80211_free_keys
   ieee80211_teardown_sdata
   ieee80211_uninit
   unregister_netdevice_many_notify
   ...
   ieee80211_if_remove

This happens when the last station of a dynamic VLAN leaves and
hostapd removes the per-VLAN interface.

Only clear the links of an AP_VLAN that is an MLD, which is the case
the original change was made for (WDS with MLO).

--- a/net/mac80211/cfg.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/cfg.c
@@ -5608,6 +5608,16 @@
 	if (wdev->iftype == NL80211_IFTYPE_AP_VLAN) {
 		int i;
 
+		/*
+		 * Only an AP_VLAN of an MLD AP shares the AP's links. A
+		 * non-MLD AP_VLAN uses its deflink as link 0, and its group
+		 * keys use link ID 0; clearing it would make
+		 * ieee80211_key_replace() fail with -ENOLINK while the keys
+		 * are freed, leaving freed keys on the key list.
+		 */
+		if (!ieee80211_vif_is_mld(&sdata->vif))
+			return;
+
 		sdata->vif.valid_links = 0;
 		sdata->vif.active_links = 0;
 		sdata->vif.dormant_links = 0;
